---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import GateExample from '../components/GateExample.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="The gates" active="gates/">
<p class="eyebrow">Quality control / Inspection station</p>
<h1>Fix the code.<br>
<span class="red">Not the threshold.</span>
</h1>
<p>Independent checks catch violations that model-level instructions may miss. This page illustrates output; it does not run a gate.</p>
<GateExample />
<section>
<h2>What gets caught.</h2>
<div class="two">
<article class="rule">
<h3>Duplicates</h3>
<p>Token-based clone detection for logic that can drift.</p>
</article>
<article class="rule">
<h3>Modularity</h3>
<p>File, function, class and export budgets.</p>
</article>
<article class="rule">
<h3>Class literals</h3>
<p>Repeated layout skeletons and design-system drift.</p>
</article>
<article class="rule">
<h3>Imports</h3>
<p>Circular dependencies and configured layer boundaries.</p>
</article>
<article class="rule">
<h3>Docs</h3>
<p>Undocumented shared exports and stale inventory.</p>
</article>
<article class="rule">
<h3>Encoding</h3>
<p>Mojibake and other encoding corruption.</p>
</article>
</div>
<p>
<a href="https://github.com/hyperbolictonic/opencode-anti-slop#how-enforcement-works">Full enforcement details ↗</a>
</p>
</section>
</SiteLayout>
